Z||000003||theogre||05-17-2000||10:06 AM||||I tried some of that black magic total shine on the plastic trim around the wipers. took off allot of the old wax residue. looks nice. It doesn't leave a really wet greasy look on things either. It also doesn't leave white crud in any fine scratches. Made all the luggage rack hardware look allot better to. (I tried it partly because it's also cheap. About $3 a bottle, compared to 6-10$ a bottle for some others.)<P>I still like Sun of a Gun for interior stuff tho. makes it look nice and protects without the greaser look the "wet" shine stuff like armorall leaves.<P>I'm using Krylon semi flat black on the mirror I'm redoing. I'll let you know how it compairs more later. At about $3 a can it's allot less expensive than most auto paint sprays.||||reg||1
